    "body": "I'm not really sure what makes more sense, but it generally seems interoperable that in the cases this change doesn't touch (i.e. cases where popstate would be after the load event anyway in Chromium and WebKit) everyone uses the order `[popstate, scroll restoration, hashchange]`: [test](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/history-traversal/scroll-restoration-order.html) [results](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/history-traversal/scroll-restoration-order.html?label=master&label=experimental&aligned).\r\n\r\nI guess we should try to expand the linked tests to also include scroll restoration if possible... seems hard though since all our traversal tests so far result in `load` being the first event.",
